# DEFI Movember — scheduled tasks
#
# INSTALLED BY `deploy/scripts/deploy.sh`, on every production deployment.
# It replaces the `deploy` user's crontab wholesale, which is the point: a
# task added by hand on the server would vanish at the next deployment
# without anyone noticing, and a task removed from this file would keep
# running for months. Either way the server and the repository would disagree
# about what is running — and the repository would be wrong.
#
# **Therefore: never edit the crontab on the server. Edit this file.**
#
# To see what is actually installed:  crontab -l
# To install it by hand:              crontab /opt/defi-movember/deploy/crontab
#
# Times are in the server's timezone. Check it with `timedatectl` — a task
# meant for 6 in the morning that runs at 4 because the server is on UTC is a
# classic, and in November it means a challenge handed out while everyone is
# asleep.

SHELL=/bin/bash
PATH=/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin

# The secret is read from the environment file at call time, never written
# here: this file is versioned in a public repository.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Disk and memory watch (story 1.11). Every ten minutes.
*/10 * * * * bash /opt/defi-movember/deploy/scripts/check-resources.sh >> /var/log/defi-movember-resources.log 2>&1

# Proof that the mechanism works (story 1.4). Once a day, at 5:07.
#
# Not on the hour, and not at midnight: everything on the internet fires at
# round o'clock, and a task that shares its minute with thousands of others
# is a task that times out for reasons of its own.
#
# It does nothing but answer. Its value is diagnostic — when a real scheduled
# task stops running in November, this line says whether cron reaches the
# application at all, which separates "the plumbing is broken" from "the task
# is broken".
7 5 * * * source /opt/defi-movember/deploy/.env.production && curl --fail --silent --show-error --max-time 30 -H "x-cron-secret: $CRON_SECRET" https://defi-movember.fr/api/cron/ping >> /var/log/defi-movember-cron.log 2>&1

# Stripe fee reconciliation (story 2.6). Every hour, at 23 past.
#
# The webhook fills in the fee within seconds in the normal case. This exists
# for the cases it cannot cover: a balance transaction Stripe had not produced
# yet, a delivery lost, the application restarting at the wrong second. Each
# of those leaves an accounting line permanently incomplete — and a line
# without its real fee is a line that cannot be reconciled against the Stripe
# statement, at the moment the association has to justify what it handed over.
#
# Hourly rather than daily: an incomplete line found in an hour is a
# non-event, one found in a week is an investigation.
23 * * * * source /opt/defi-movember/deploy/.env.production && curl --fail --silent --show-error --max-time 60 -H "x-cron-secret: $CRON_SECRET" https://defi-movember.fr/api/cron/rapprochement >> /var/log/defi-movember-cron.log 2>&1

# The day's challenges (story 4.4). Every morning at 5:04, Paris time.
#
# Before anyone is awake, and not on the hour: everything on the internet
# fires at a round o'clock, and a task sharing its minute with thousands of
# others is a task that times out for reasons of its own.
#
# ⚠️ The application computes the date in Europe/Paris, not from the server's
# clock. A VPS on UTC would otherwise turn "the challenge of 1 November" into
# something handed out at one in the morning on 31 October — and nobody would
# notice until a participant said their challenge had changed overnight.
#
# Re-running it is harmless, at any hour: participants who already have a
# challenge are skipped, the draw is deterministic, and the database refuses a
# second one. If a morning goes wrong, run this line by hand and move on.
4 5 * * * source /opt/defi-movember/deploy/.env.production && curl --fail --silent --show-error --max-time 120 -H "x-cron-secret: $CRON_SECRET" https://defi-movember.fr/api/cron/defis-du-jour >> /var/log/defi-movember-cron.log 2>&1

# Provider token renewal (story 3.7). Every hour, at 41 past.
#
# A Strava access token lasts a few hours. Without this line, every link made
# during the game dies overnight, and each participant discovers it by losing
# a challenge — three days later, with no way to connect the two events.
#
# It renews ahead of need: a token expiring within ninety minutes is taken by
# THIS run rather than the next, so nothing dies in the gap between two.
#
# Re-running it is harmless. A link already renewed is no longer due, and a
# claim taken before each provider call stops two runs from invalidating each
# other's refresh token.
41 * * * * source /opt/defi-movember/deploy/.env.production && curl --fail --silent --show-error --max-time 120 -H "x-cron-secret: $CRON_SECRET" https://defi-movember.fr/api/cron/jetons >> /var/log/defi-movember-cron.log 2>&1

# Strava catch-up (story 3.6). Every hour, at 17 past.
#
# ⚠️ On the environment WITHOUT the webhook subscription, this is not a safety
# net — it is the only way activities arrive. Strava allows one subscription
# per application, so preproduction and production cannot both have it.
#
# Where the webhook does run, this catches what it lost: a delivery failed, a
# service restarted, a deployment in the middle of a Sunday morning. It looks
# two days back, so an outage over a night is covered.
#
# Re-running it is harmless: the database refuses an activity it already has,
# and only newly stored ones are evaluated.
17 * * * * source /opt/defi-movember/deploy/.env.production && curl --fail --silent --show-error --max-time 300 -H "x-cron-secret: $CRON_SECRET" https://defi-movember.fr/api/cron/rattrapage >> /var/log/defi-movember-cron.log 2>&1

# Leaderboards (story 7.3). Every fifteen minutes, offset from the quarter.
#
# Nothing computes a ranking on demand: all eight come from one materialised
# view, and this is what keeps it current. A ranking recomputed on every page
# load, for 800 participants, would be both expensive and unstable — and this
# is a screen people open several times a day.
#
# Fifteen minutes of lag is irrelevant in a game that lasts a month. A
# leaderboard that takes four seconds to open is not.
#
# Re-running it is harmless, and two runs never collide: the function takes an
# advisory lock and the second one gives up rather than queueing behind the
# first. Two of these piling up is how a small delay becomes an outage.
3,18,33,48 * * * * source /opt/defi-movember/deploy/.env.production && curl --fail --silent --show-error --max-time 120 -H "x-cron-secret: $CRON_SECRET" https://defi-movember.fr/api/cron/classements >> /var/log/defi-movember-cron.log 2>&1

# Business tasks arrive with their epics:
#   - backups ............................. epic 11
